        </details>
      </div>
      <div class="hint">Item counts are caps; DailyDigest will show fewer when there are not enough strong candidates.</div>
    </div>

    <details class="step settings-disclosure" id="summary-options"{% if errors %} open{% endif %}>
      {% set summary_labels = {"extractive": "Local extractive", "api": "OpenAI-compatible API", "anthropic": "Anthropic Claude API", "claude_cli": "Signed-in Claude Code", "codex_cli": "Signed-in Codex"} %}
      <summary>How to summarize
        <span class="disclosure-note">Current choice: <span id="summary-current">{{ summary_labels.get(form.llm_backend, "Local extractive") }}</span></span>
      </summary>
      <p class="hint">Native mode can use local commands and configured providers directly. Browser mode can reach APIs directly or through the browser companion; signed-in CLI commands need a connected companion. Extractive summaries stay on this device in either mode.</p>
      <div class="backends">
        <label class="backend-opt" data-value="extractive">
          <input type="radio" name="llm_backend" value="extractive"
                 {% if form.llm_backend == "extractive" %}checked{% endif %}>
          <strong>Extractive</strong> — recommended for the first run.
          <div class="desc">Free. No account, API key, or paid AI subscription.</div>
        </label>

        <label class="backend-opt" data-value="api">
          <input type="radio" name="llm_backend" value="api"
                 {% if form.llm_backend == "api" %}checked{% endif %}>
          <strong>OpenAI-compatible API</strong> — optional richer summaries.
          <div class="desc">OpenAI, OpenRouter, Ollama, vLLM, or another compatible endpoint. Online providers use separate API billing.</div>
        </label>

        <label class="backend-opt" data-value="anthropic">
          <input type="radio" name="llm_backend" value="anthropic"
                 {% if form.llm_backend == "anthropic" %}checked{% endif %}>
          <strong>Anthropic Claude API</strong> — native Messages API.
          <div class="desc">Uses an Anthropic Console API key and API billing; a Claude chat subscription is not an API key.</div>
        </label>

        <label class="backend-opt" data-value="claude_cli">
          <input type="radio" name="llm_backend" value="claude_cli"
                 {% if form.llm_backend == "claude_cli" %}checked{% endif %}>
          <strong>Signed-in Claude Code</strong> — use your local Claude login.
          <div class="desc">Requires the <code>claude</code> command to be installed and signed in. Tools and session persistence are disabled for summaries.</div>
        </label>

        <label class="backend-opt" data-value="codex_cli">
          <input type="radio" name="llm_backend" value="codex_cli"
                 {% if form.llm_backend == "codex_cli" %}checked{% endif %}>
          <strong>Signed-in Codex</strong> — use your local ChatGPT/Codex login.
          <div class="desc">Requires the <code>codex</code> command to be installed and signed in. Runs ephemerally, read-only, with agent tools disabled.</div>
        </label>
      </div>

      <details class="settings-disclosure"><summary>What is sent for AI summaries?</summary>
        <p class="hint">Your chosen provider receives selected article titles, sources, sections, dates, internal item IDs, abstract excerpts (up to 1,500 characters), and derived contribution, claim and evidence labels. Personalization includes the first 400 characters of your current research or learning goal and up to 20 core topics; derived labels may also name your configured topics. Catch-up briefings include up to 60 titles and sources and the number of days away. Extractive stays local.</p>
      </details>

      <div class="api-fields" id="api-fields"{% if form.llm_backend == "extractive" %} hidden{% endif %}>
        <div id="api-auth-fields"{% if form.llm_backend not in ["api", "anthropic"] %} hidden{% endif %}>
          <label for="llm_base_url">Base URL</label>
          <input type="url" id="llm_base_url" name="llm_base_url"
                 placeholder="https://api.openai.com/v1" value="{{ form.llm_base_url }}">
          <label for="llm_api_key">API key</label>
          <input type="password" id="llm_api_key" name="llm_api_key"
                 placeholder="Provider API key" value="{{ form.llm_api_key }}">
          {% if form.llm_api_key %}
          <label class="hint" for="remove_llm_api_key">
            <input type="checkbox" id="remove_llm_api_key" name="remove_llm_api_key"
                   value="true" {% if form.remove_llm_api_key == "true" %}checked{% endif %}>
            Remove the saved API key
          </label>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
        <label for="llm_model">Model</label>
        <input type="text" id="llm_model" name="llm_model"
               placeholder="gpt-4o-mini" value="{{ form.llm_model }}">
        <div class="hint" id="provider-hint"></div>
        <div id="connection-check-controls">
          <button class="btn" type="button" id="test-api-connection">Test API connection</button>
          <p class="hint" id="connection-check-note">Only when clicked: sends a small test to this API, which may be billed. Testing does not save settings.</p>
          <p class="hint" id="connection-check-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>

    <div class="settings-actions">
      <p class="hint" id="settings-save-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">{% if errors %}Changes have not been saved. Correct the highlighted fields.{% else %}Changes take effect after saving.{% endif %}</p>
      <button class="brew" type="submit" name="after_save" value="{{ 'brew' if first_run | default(not form.topics) else 'save' }}">{{ 'Brew' if first_run | default(not form.topics) else 'Save changes' }}</button>
    </div>
  </form>
</div>
{% endblock %}
{% block scripts %}
<script>
(function () {
  const topics = document.getElementById("topics");
  const details = document.getElementById("topic-details");
  const rows = document.getElementById("interest-rows");
  const editor = document.getElementById("interest-editor");
  const firstUse = {{ 'true' if first_run | default(not form.topics) else 'false' }};
  let metadata = {};
  try { metadata = JSON.parse(details.value || "{}"); } catch (_) {}
  const spellingCache = new Map();
  let spellingQueue = Promise.resolve(), lastSpellingStart = 0;
  function lookupSpelling(topic, signal) {
    const task = spellingQueue.then(async () => {
      if (signal.aborted) throw new DOMException('Cancelled', 'AbortError');
      if (spellingCache.has(topic)) return spellingCache.get(topic);
      const delay = Math.max(0, 350 - (Date.now() - lastSpellingStart));
      if (delay) await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, delay));
      if (signal.aborted) throw new DOMException('Cancelled', 'AbortError');
      lastSpellingStart = Date.now();
      const response = await fetch('/setup/check-wording?' + new URLSearchParams({topic}), {
        method: 'POST', signal,
        headers: {'X-CSRF-Token': topics.form.querySelector('[name="_csrf_token"]').value},
      });
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Spelling unavailable');
      const result = await response.json();
      if (result.topic !== topic) throw new Error('Unexpected spelling response');
      spellingCache.set(topic, result.suggestion || null);
      return result.suggestion || null;
    });
    spellingQueue = task.catch(() => {});
    return task;
  }
  function percentages(weights, total = 100) {
    const count = weights.length;
    if (!count) return [];
    const sum = weights.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
    if (!(sum > 0)) return percentages(weights.map(() => 1), total);
    const raw = weights.map(weight => total * weight / sum);
    const allocated = raw.map(weight => Math.max(1, Math.floor(weight)));
    let difference = total - allocated.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
    // A forced 1% minimum has already received its rounding point.
    const order = raw.map((weight, index) => ({index, fraction: weight - allocated[index]})).sort((a, b) => b.fraction - a.fraction || a.index - b.index);
    for (let i = 0; difference > 0; i++, difference--) allocated[order[i % count].index]++;
    // Very small legacy weights can require the 1% floor. Remove those
    // extra points from the most overallocated remaining interests.
    while (difference < 0) {
      const index = allocated.map((weight, index) => ({index, excess: weight - raw[index]})).filter(row => allocated[row.index] > 1).sort((a, b) => b.excess - a.excess || a.index - b.index)[0].index;
      allocated[index]--; difference++;
    }
    return allocated;
  }
  let baselineFormState = null;
  let rowSequence = 0, weightsEdited = false, weightsTouched = false, loadedCount = 0, activeRow = null, removedTopic = null;
  function serialize() {
    const result = [], data = Object.create(null);
    const allRows = [...rows.children];
    const preserveRaw = !weightsTouched && allRows.length === loadedCount && allRows.every(row => row.dataset.rawWeight !== undefined);
    for (const row of allRows) {
      const name = row.querySelector('[data-interest-name]').value.trim();
      const weight = preserveRaw ? row.dataset.rawWeight : row.querySelector('[data-interest-weight]').value;
      const title = row.querySelector('[data-interest-title]');
      if (title) title.textContent = name || 'New topic';
      if (name) {
        result.push(`${name} | ${weight}`);
        data[name] = {aliases: row.querySelector('[data-interest-aliases]').value.split(/[;\r\n]+/).map(term => term.trim()).filter(Boolean), description: row.querySelector('[data-interest-description]').value.trim()};
        if (row.dataset.correctedFrom) data[name].previous_name = row.dataset.correctedFrom;
      }
    }
    topics.value = result.join('\n'); details.value = JSON.stringify(data);
    document.getElementById('topic-weight-mode').value = preserveRaw ? 'relative' : 'percentage';
    const inputs = [...rows.querySelectorAll('[data-interest-weight]')];
    const sum = inputs.reduce((total, input) => total + Number(input.value || 0), 0);
    const individuallyValid = inputs.every(input => Number.isInteger(Number(input.value)) && Number(input.value) >= 1 && Number(input.value) <= 101 - inputs.length);
    const valid = sum === 100 && individuallyValid;
    editor.classList.toggle('single-topic', inputs.length === 1 && valid);
    const reminder = sum < 100 ? ` · ${100 - sum}% left to assign` : sum > 100 ? ` · ${sum - 100}% over` : ' · use whole percentages';
    document.getElementById('interest-total').textContent = valid ? '' : `Total: ${sum}%${reminder}`;
    inputs.forEach(input => { input.max = String(101 - inputs.length); input.setCustomValidity(''); });
    if (inputs.length && individuallyValid && !valid) inputs[0].setCustomValidity('Use whole-number percentages totaling 100%. Choose Normalize to 100% to adjust the shares.');
    document.getElementById('add-interest').disabled = rows.children.length >= 10;
    if (baselineFormState !== null) markUnsaved();
  }
  function finishEditing(row, keep = true) {
    if (!row) return true;
    const name = row.querySelector('[data-interest-name]');
    if (keep && !name.checkValidity()) { name.reportValidity(); return false; }
    if (!keep) row.cancelSpelling?.();
    if (!keep && row.creationSnapshot) {
      const snapshot = row.creationSnapshot; row.remove(); activeRow = null;
      for (const [existing, weight] of snapshot.weights) if (existing.isConnected) existing.querySelector('[data-interest-weight]').value = weight;
      weightsTouched = snapshot.touched; weightsEdited = snapshot.edited; serialize();
      document.getElementById('add-interest').focus(); return true;
    }
    if (!keep && row.editSnapshot) {
      for (const [selector, value] of Object.entries(row.editSnapshot.fields)) row.querySelector(selector).value = value;
      if (row.editSnapshot.previousName) row.dataset.correctedFrom = row.editSnapshot.previousName;
      else delete row.dataset.correctedFrom;
      name.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', {bubbles: true}));
      row.cancelSpelling?.();
    }
    if (keep) row.checkSpelling?.();
    row.querySelector('.interest-name-field').hidden = true;
    row.querySelector('[data-interest-title]').hidden = false;
    row.querySelector('.interest-edit-panel').hidden = true;
    row.querySelector('[data-interest-edit]').setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
    row.querySelector('[data-interest-edit]').hidden = false;
    row.querySelector('[data-interest-remove]').hidden = true;
    if (activeRow === row) activeRow = null;
    delete row.creationSnapshot; serialize(); return true;
  }
  function beginEditing(row, focus = true) {
    if (activeRow && activeRow !== row && !finishEditing(activeRow)) return false;
    if (activeRow !== row) row.editSnapshot = {fields: Object.fromEntries(['[data-interest-name]', '[data-interest-aliases]', '[data-interest-description]'].map(selector => [selector, row.querySelector(selector).value])), previousName: row.dataset.correctedFrom || ''};
    activeRow = row;
    row.querySelector('.interest-name-field').hidden = false;
    row.querySelector('[data-interest-title]').hidden = true;
    row.querySelector('.interest-edit-panel').hidden = false;
    row.querySelector('[data-interest-edit]').setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
    row.querySelector('[data-interest-edit]').hidden = true;
    row.querySelector('[data-interest-remove]').hidden = false;
    if (focus) row.querySelector('[data-interest-name]').focus();
    return true;
  }
  function forgetAdditionWeights() { [...rows.children].forEach(row => { delete row.additionSnapshot; }); }
  function commitPriority(input) {
    const value = Number(input.value), others = [...rows.querySelectorAll('[data-interest-weight]')].filter(field => field !== input);
    if (!Number.isInteger(value) || value < 1 || value > 100 - others.length || (!others.length && value !== 100)) { serialize(); return; }
    if (others.length) percentages(others.map(field => Math.max(1, Number(field.value) || 1)), 100 - value).forEach((weight, index) => { others[index].value = weight; });
    weightsTouched = true; weightsEdited = true; serialize();
  }
  function addRow(name = '', weight = 100, detail = {}) {
    const row = document.createElement('div'); row.className = 'interest-row';
    const originalFacetName = detail.previous_name || name;
    if (detail.previous_name) row.dataset.correctedFrom = detail.previous_name;
    // This markup is constant; reader text is assigned through .value only.
    row.innerHTML = '<div class="interest-heading"><div><span class="interest-title" data-interest-title></span><label class="interest-name-field" hidden>Topic<input data-interest-name type="text" required maxlength="160" placeholder="e.g. battery materials or galaxy formation"></label></div><label class="interest-weight-label"><span class="sr-only">Priority percentage</span><span class="interest-weight-wrap"><input data-interest-weight type="number" min="1" max="100" step="1" required><span aria-hidden="true">%</span></span></label><button class="interest-edit-button" data-interest-edit type="button" aria-expanded="false">Edit</button><button class="interest-remove-button" data-interest-remove type="button" hidden>Remove</button></div><div class="interest-edit-panel" hidden><details class="topic-aliases"><summary>Other names (optional)</summary><label><span class="sr-only">Other names, one per line</span><textarea data-interest-aliases rows="2" maxlength="500" placeholder="e.g. quantum error correction&#10;QEC"></textarea></label><label class="saved-topic-focus" hidden>Saved focus<textarea data-interest-description maxlength="600"></textarea></label></details></div>';
    const number = ++rowSequence;
    for (const [selector, label] of [['[data-interest-name]', 'Research topic'], ['[data-interest-weight]', 'Priority percentage'], ['[data-interest-aliases]', 'Other names']]) {
      row.querySelector(selector).setAttribute('aria-label', `${label} ${number}`);
    }
    const editButton = row.querySelector('[data-interest-edit]');
    editButton.setAttribute('aria-label', `Edit research topic ${number}`);
